-- title:
--   Blockwise decoding of an ordered global output record
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $h,J$. Let $L_h$ be the ordered list of local records, each pairing a schedule occurrence with a $2h$-element output subset of a $512h$-element block, and let $m=\operatorname{scheduleSize}(h)\operatorname{layerCount}(h)$ be its length. The list $G_{h,J}$ enumerates the ordered Cartesian power of these local records.
--
--   For $k<m^J$ and a coordinate $j<J$, let $d_j$ be coordinate $j$ of the length-$J$ base-$m$ digit list of $k$, with the most significant digit first. Then
--   $$
--   G_{h,J}[k](j)=L_h[d_j].
--   $$
--   The formal statement uses defaulted list lookup; the stated bounds ensure that the entries used are in range.
--
--   This connects a physical global-record index to the original local occurrence and mask at each block.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/OutputDecodeRecords.lean#L82-L98

